Disney says its plans to merge Disney+ and Hulu will be completed in December, with subscribers able to have a "fully unified experience" on Disney+ with Hulu live TV and premium add-ons.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-909605" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2023/09/disney.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" /><br/>
The detail was included in Disney's <a href="https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1744489/000174448926000065/fy2026_q4xerxex991.htm">fourth quarter earnings report</a>. Disney believes the unified app will make it easier for customers to find content across the Disney brands and franchises.<br/>
<br/>
Disney first announced plans to combine Disney+ and Hulu into one streaming service <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2023/05/11/disney-plus-hulu-combo-app/">in May 2023</a>, so the process has taken over three years. Disney has controlled Hulu since 2019, and it paid about &#36;9 billion to buy out Comcast in a deal that closed in 2025.<br/>
<br/>
